## 3. Trade-offs & Architectural Decisions

| Architectural Choice | Decision Made | Trade-Off / Alternative Considered |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Reverse Proxy Layer** | Nginx Alpine Container | Traefik or Envoy offer dynamic service discovery, but Nginx is the industry gold standard for static file performance, battle-tested stability, and zero memory footprint (~15MB RAM). |
| **Asset Delivery** | Nginx serves compiled SPA `dist/` directly | Serving React via Node.js dev server (`vite preview`) consumes 150MB+ RAM and blocks Node's event loop with static I/O. Nginx uses kernel-level `sendfile` for zero-copy file transfer. |
| **Worker Container Access** | Mount `/var/run/docker.sock` | Docker-in-Docker (dind) runs a nested Docker daemon inside the worker container (requires `--privileged` mode). Mounting `/var/run/docker.sock` ("Docker-out-of-Docker") uses the host daemon with much lower overhead. |
| **Nginx Header Inheritance** | Explicit security headers on `server` and `location` blocks | In Nginx, adding an `add_header` directive inside a `location` block completely disables inheritance of all `add_header` directives from parent blocks. Explicit declaration ensures headers are never dropped. |

